<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0f1117;
    --card: #1a1d27;
    --card-hover: #22263a;
    --accent: #4f8cff;
    --accent2: #ff6b6b;
    --accent3: #ffd93d;
    --accent4: #6bcb77;
    --text: #e0e0e0;
    --text-muted: #8a8fa8;
    --border: #2a2e3f;
    --red: #ff4757;
    --orange: #ffa502;
    --green: #2ed573;
    --iran: #8e44ad;
  }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.65; }
  .container { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }

  .hero { text-align: center; padding: 56px 20px 36px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1d27 0%, #0f1117 100%); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .hero h1 { font-size: 2.2em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent), var(--accent2)); -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; }
  .hero .subtitle { font-size: 1em; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto 16px; }
  .hero .date-badge { display: inline-block; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--accent); }
  .hero .war-day { display: inline-block; background: var(--accent2); color: #fff; border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: 600; margin-left: 8px; }
  .hero .build-meta { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .triplet-badge { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #0e1a1e); border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 8px; padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--accent); display: inline-block; margin-top: 10px; }

  .direction-of-travel { max-width: 900px; margin: 24px auto; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #1a1d27); border: 2px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 12px; padding: 22px 28px; font-size: 1.05em; line-height: 1.55; }
  .direction-of-travel .label { font-size: 0.72em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .direction-of-travel .body { color: var(--text); }
  .direction-of-travel .body .cite { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.92em; }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move { border-color: var(--border); }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move .body { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }

  .disclaimer { background: #2a1a1a; border: 1px solid #5a2020; border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 24px auto; max-width: 900px; font-size: 0.85em; color: #ffaaaa; }
  .disclaimer strong { color: var(--accent2); }

  .section { padding: 30px 0; }
  .section-title { font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; }
  .section-title .meta { font-size: 0.6em; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 400; }

  /* === FORECAST BOARD === */
  .forecast-board { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label { font-size: 0.75em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 14px 0 4px; padding-left: 4px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .forecast-card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; }
  .forecast-card.cat-diplomacy { border-left-color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card.cat-military { border-left-color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card.cat-regime { border-left-color: var(--iran); }
  .forecast-card.cat-market { border-left-color: var(--accent3); }
  .forecast-card.cat-domestic { border-left-color: var(--accent4); }
  .forecast-card.cat-humanitarian { border-left-color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-id { font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.7em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-category { font-size: 0.7em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 4px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-question { font-size: 1em; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; line-height: 1.45; }
  .forecast-card .fc-probrow { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 18px; margin-bottom: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.8em; font-weight: 800; color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta { font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-up { color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-down { color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.no-move { color: var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-horizon { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta-reason { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 4px 12px; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dd { color: var(--text); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicators { font-size: 0.82em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 6px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; margin: 2px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-OBSERVED { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); border-color: var(--green); color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-PARTIAL { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); border-color: var(--orange); color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-CONTRADICTED { background: rgba(255, 71, 87, 0.15); border-color: var(--red); color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-NOT_OBSERVED { color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE { opacity: 0.55; border-left-style: dashed; }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE .fc-question::after { content: ' [OBE]'; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }
  .forecast-empty-slot { background: transparent; border: 1px dashed var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === DELTA SECTION === */
  .delta-narrative p { color: var(--text); font-size: 0.96em; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .delta-narrative p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.88em; }
  .delta-narrative p .context-only { color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }

  /* === SCENARIO MAP === */
  .scenario-map { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .prob-bar-container { display: flex; height: 36px; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; margin: 8px 0 14px; }
  .prob-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.85em; color: #fff; }
  .prob-escalation { background: var(--red); }
  .prob-status { background: var(--orange); }
  .prob-deescalation { background: var(--green); }
  .scenario-line { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .scenario-line strong.label-esc { color: var(--red); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-prot { color: var(--orange); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-desc { color: var(--green); }

  /* === INSIDE IRAN === */
  .inside-iran { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .inside-iran p { font-size: 0.93em; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .inside-iran p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .iran-media-badges { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .iran-media-badge { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.72em; color: var(--iran); }

  /* === REGIME CHANGE WATCH === */
  .regime-watch { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .regime-watch-meta { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .regime-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .regime-row:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .regime-row .name { font-weight: 600; }
  .regime-row .p { font-size: 1.4em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--orange); }
  .regime-row .drivers { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); flex-basis: 100%; margin-top: 4px; }

  /* === SOURCES === */
  .sources-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .sources-list li { padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 0.88em; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .sources-list a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .sources-list a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .source-tier { display: inline-block; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.7em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.5px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .source-tier.tier-TIER1 { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); color: var(--green); border: 1px solid var(--green); }
  .source-tier.tier-OSINT { background: rgba(79, 140, 255, 0.15); color: var(--accent); border: 1px solid var(--accent); }
  .source-tier.tier-STATE_MEDIA { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); color: var(--orange); border: 1px solid var(--orange); }
  .source-tier.tier-EXPERT { background: rgba(155, 89, 182, 0.15); color: #9b59b6; border: 1px solid #9b59b6; }

  /* === EXPERT APPENDIX === */
  .expert-appendix { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; margin-top: 18px; }
  .expert-appendix summary { padding: 14px 20px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.92em; user-select: none; }
  .expert-appendix summary:hover { color: var(--text); }
  .expert-appendix[open] summary { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 20px 18px; }
  .expert-quote { padding: 10px 14px; border-left: 3px solid #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 0.9em; }
  .expert-quote .expert-name { font-weight: 700; color: #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .expert-empty { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === FOOTER === */
  footer { text-align: center; padding: 32px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.8em; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin-top: 32px; }
  footer .next-update { color: var(--accent); }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .hero { padding: 36px 16px 24px; }
    .hero h1 { font-size: 1.5em; line-height: 1.3; }
    .container { padding: 12px; }
    .direction-of-travel { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 16px 18px; font-size: 0.95em; }
    .disclaimer { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 12px; font-size: 0.8em; }
    .section-title { font-size: 1.2em; }
    .forecast-card { padding: 14px 16px; }
    .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.5em; }
    .scenario-map, .inside-iran, .regime-watch, .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 16px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="hero">
  <h1>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Forecast board + descriptive delta. Predictions are time-bounded and scored; descriptions are sourced and verb-disciplined.</p>
  <span class="date-badge">May 23, 2026</span>
  <span class="war-day">Day 85 of Operation Epic Fury</span>
  <div class="build-meta">Published: <span id="pub-ts">2026-05-23T09:00:00+02:00</span> · Build <span id="build-id" style="font-family:monospace;opacity:0.6;">v45.2</span></div>
  <div class="triplet-badge">⚖ Triple-blind: Analyst + Devil's Advocate + Judge · forecast-board v45</div>
</div>

<div class="container">

  <!-- ========== 1. DIRECTION OF TRAVEL ========== -->
  <div class="direction-of-travel">
    <div class="label">Where this is heading</div>
    <div class="body">
      Iran's PGSA jurisdiction claim over UAE and Oman waters drives <span class="cite">F1</span> (Hormuz shipping) further from resolution, while the fifth Rome round's explicit "deep and significant gaps" declaration narrows the window for <span class="cite">F3</span> (Iran-US deal by June 5); domestically, the Knesset's 110-0 preliminary dissolution vote has materially raised the probability that <span class="cite">F5</span> resolves YES before June 1.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="disclaimer">
    <strong>⚠ DISCLAIMER:</strong> This analysis relies on open sources (OSINT) and AI-generated assessments. Probabilities are time-bounded forecasts with resolution criteria; track record visible internally until ≥20 forecasts resolve. Descriptive sections enforce verb discipline — any causal/directional claim must cite a forecast or be marked context-only.
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 2. FORECAST BOARD ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="forecast-board">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Forecast Board
      <span class="meta">6 active · 1 resolved today (F4) · last reasoned 2026-05-23</span>
    </h2>

    <div class="forecast-board">

      <!-- NEAR-TERM (≤72h) -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">Near-Term (≤72h)</div>
      <div class="forecast-empty-slot">No publishable forecast in this horizon today.</div>

      <!-- 7-30 DAYS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">7–30 Days</div>

      <!-- F5 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-domestic status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F5 · 2026-05-19-netanyahu-early-election-by-june-1</span>
          <span class="fc-category">domestic</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Netanyahu formally announce an early election date earlier than the mandatory 2026-10-27 date before EOD 2026-06-01?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">32%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-up">▲ +10pp from 22% (2026-05-19)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-06-01</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Updated 0.22 → 0.32. The government-backed Knesset dissolution bill passed its preliminary reading 110-0 on May 20 (Times of Israel, Haaretz, Jerusalem Post), with Netanyahu absent. The bill does not yet set an election date and requires committee review plus three legislative readings. Netanyahu reportedly prefers October and is attempting side-deals with Haredi parties. However, the 110-0 unanimous margin with both coalition and opposition in agreement is a qualitatively new development — it is now the legislature's direction, not a threat. A formal announcement by Netanyahu before June 1 remains distinct from this process proceeding.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if Netanyahu makes a formal Knesset speech or public announcement naming an election date earlier than 2026-10-27; OR if the Knesset passes a formal dissolution motion by majority vote. Leaks and media speculation do NOT resolve.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Times of Israel, Haaretz, or Channel 12/13 citing direct Netanyahu statement or official Knesset vote record. Reuters/AP confirmation required for international sources.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Coalition partner threatening dissolution without a formal Knesset vote = NOT resolved. Netanyahu 'considering' elections per aides = NOT resolved. Only a formal announcement by Netanyahu himself or a passed dissolution vote counts.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Degel HaTorah files formal no-confidence motion in Knesset</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-PARTIAL">Knesset dissolution bill advances past second reading [preliminary reading passed 110-0, May 20]</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- N2 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-domestic status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N2 · 2026-05-23-knesset-dissolution-bill-final-reading-by-june-01</span>
          <span class="fc-category">domestic</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the Knesset dissolution bill (passed 110-0 in preliminary reading May 20) complete its final (third) reading and achieve legally binding dissolution before EOD 2026-06-01?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">35%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">— new forecast</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-06-01</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Initial assignment. The dissolution bill requires committee review and three legislative readings after the May 20 preliminary. Ultra-Orthodox parties favor an accelerated timeline (September elections); Netanyahu prefers October and is seeking side-deals to delay. The 110-0 margin removes ambiguity about the legislature's direction, but Netanyahu retains procedural tools to slow committee scheduling. Nine days to horizon; Israel's fractious legislative process rarely compresses this fast without extraordinary pressure.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if the Knesset holds and passes a third-reading dissolution vote by majority before EOD 2026-06-01. NO if the bill has not reached third reading by that date.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Knesset official record confirmed by Times of Israel, Haaretz, or Jerusalem Post reporting on the specific third-reading vote outcome.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Committee approval alone without third-reading floor vote = NOT resolved. First or second reading passage = NOT resolved. Only the final dissolution vote counts. If bill is withdrawn or tabled = RESOLVE-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Knesset House Committee schedules second reading within 72h of May 23</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Netanyahu-Haredi side deal announced, halting dissolution process</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- F3 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F3 · 2026-05-19-iran-us-deal-signed-by-june-5</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Iran and the US confirm a signed written framework agreement (any named successor to the 14-point MOU) before EOD 2026-06-05?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">20%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">▼ −5pp from 25% (2026-05-19)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-06-05</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Updated 0.25 → 0.20. The fifth round of US-Iran talks concluded in Rome on May 23 without a breakthrough. Araghchi stated publicly that "deep and significant gaps" remain with Washington (Kaieteur News, citing Iranian FM). The Omani mediator reported "some but not conclusive progress." Araghchi told UN Secretary-General Guterres that US "excessive demands" are the main obstacle. IRNA quoted FM spokesman Baghaei confirming nuclear enrichment details "are not being discussed at this stage" — structurally incompatible with the US demand for verifiable denuclearization. No Witkoff/Araghchi direct meeting confirmed; talks remain Omani-mediated. With 13 days to horizon and gaps explicitly described as "deep and significant" after five rounds, the probability of a signed framework is reduced.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if a named US administration official AND a named Iranian official publicly confirm a signed written framework (by any name); OR if the document text is published by Axios/Reuters/State Dept or Iran MFA with both parties acknowledging authenticity. Verbal 'agreement in principle' does not count.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>At minimum, Reuters AND one of Axios/AP/AFP quoting named US AND Iranian principals (not envoys alone). Official Iranian Foreign Ministry statement or State Dept press release also resolves.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Agreement by envoys only, without principal confirmation (Trump/Pezeshkian) within 72h of announcement = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. If Iran signs but Khamenei's office disavows within 72h = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Witkoff/Araghchi direct meeting confirmed (not via Pakistan or Oman)</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Trump public statement calling deal 'beautiful' or 'done'</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 30-90 DAYS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">30–90 Days</div>

      <!-- F1 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-market status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F1 · 2026-05-11-hormuz-commercial-shipping-resumed-by-june-10</span>
          <span class="fc-category">market</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will at least 50 commercial vessels per day transit the Strait of Hormuz (50%+ of pre-war ~120/day baseline) during any consecutive 7-day window before EOD 2026-06-10?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">30%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">▼ −8pp from 38% (2026-05-19)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-06-10</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Updated 0.38 → 0.30. On May 22, only 2 independently verified commercial vessels transited the strait (Hormuz Strait Monitor), against a pre-war baseline of 95/day. Lloyd's war-risk premiums remain at 5%+ of hull value — far above the 1.5% indicator threshold. Iran's Persian Gulf Strait Authority (PGSA) on May 22 formally claimed jurisdiction over UAE and Oman sovereign waters at both strait entrances; Bahrain, Kuwait, Qatar, Saudi Arabia, and the UAE immediately responded with a joint IMO letter urging vessels not to engage with PGSA. The IRGC self-reported 35 PGSA-cleared transits in 24h, but independent verification (Windward.ai, Lloyd's List) identifies these as shadow-fleet vessels. Maersk, MSC, and Frontline have not announced any return to scheduled Hormuz transits.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if Hormuz Strait Monitor (or UNCTAD, or Lloyd's List) reports ≥50 daily transits averaged over 7 consecutive days within the horizon window. NO if average stays below 50/day for the full horizon window.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Hormuz Strait Monitor (primary), Lloyd's List Intelligence (secondary), UNCTAD Maritime Trade quarterly report (lagging confirmation).</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>If only Iranian-flagged or sanctions-evading dark-fleet vessels make up the count but Western insurers still refuse: AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. PGSA addendum: third-country vessels count ONLY IF ≥2 of Hormuz Strait Monitor/Lloyd's List/UNCTAD/Windward confirm them as independent commercial entities not under IRGC-linked tolls; PGSA self-reported numbers excluded.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Lloyd's war-risk premium reduced below 1.5% of hull</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Maersk/MSC/Frontline announce return to scheduled Hormuz transit</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- N1 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-market status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N1 · 2026-05-23-pgsa-first-verified-neutral-transit-by-june-10</span>
          <span class="fc-category">market</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Iran's Persian Gulf Strait Authority (PGSA) toll regime receive at least one publicly confirmed, independently verified transit by a non-sanctioned, non-Iranian commercial vessel before EOD 2026-06-10?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">22%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">— new forecast</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-06-10</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Initial assignment. Iran's PGSA formally claimed jurisdiction over UAE and Oman sovereign waters on May 22, with a functioning permit application system (info@PGSA.ir) and reported transit fees up to $2 million paid in Chinese yuan. IRGC self-reports claim 35 coordinated passages in 24h, but Windward.ai and Lloyd's List identify these as predominantly shadow-fleet vessels under IRGC-linked ownership. Bahrain, Kuwait, Qatar, Saudi Arabia, and the UAE filed a joint IMO letter opposing PGSA engagement. A confirmed non-sanctioned Chinese, Indian, or Turkish vessel completing a PGSA-permitted transit and verified by Windward/Lloyd's List is plausible but faces compliance and reputational barriers.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if Windward.ai, Lloyd's List, or UNCTAD confirms via AIS/satellite tracking that ≥1 non-sanctioned, non-Iranian-flagged commercial vessel completed a full Strait of Hormuz transit after registering with PGSA. NO if no such independently verified transit occurs before EOD 2026-06-10.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Windward.ai AIS analysis OR Lloyd's List Intelligence vessel tracking; OR named company press release acknowledging PGSA-cleared transit. IRGC/PGSA self-reports alone do NOT resolve YES.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Vessel transiting without PGSA permit but waved through by IRGC = NOT counted. Iranian-linked entities using third-country flags = NOT counted. If vessel ownership is disputed, AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
