      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path:</strong> Talks continue past June 5 without a signed framework, Hormuz remains below 5% of baseline through June 10 (F1 resolves NO), and Israeli domestic politics extend into a September–October election cycle as Netanyahu delays the dissolution bill's final readings.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path:</strong> A sixth Omani-mediated round produces an MOU by late May/early June (F3 resolves YES), insurance markets respond with premium reductions below 3%, and Maersk conditionally resumes Hormuz transits under US escort.</p>
